      "guide.reply.bye":"Bye for now — have fun exploring! 💚",
      "guide.reply.importance":"Happy to share — the Presidents’ Memorabilia preserves artifacts such as commemorative trophies, plaques, and travel souvenirs that embody the Lasallian values and leadership of DLSU-D’s former presidents. As a historical link between the community’s past and future, the collection supports the university’s identity as a Heritage and Cultural Center.",
      "guide.reply.visit":"You’re welcome anytime — Sulyap Lasalyano helps students, faculty, staff, and visitors discover and appreciate DLSU-D’s institutional heritage—onsite at the Presidents’ Memorabilia in AEA-IRC, or through this digital experience in a mobile browser.",
      "guide.reply.maintain":"Here’s the scoop — the collection is housed at the Aklatang Emilio Aguinaldo – Information Resource Center (AEA-IRC) of De La Salle University-Dasmariñas, a fitting home for the Presidents’ Memorabilia as part of DLSU-D’s Heritage and Cultural Center identity.",
      "guide.reply.what":"Glad you asked! Sulyap Lasalyano is a web-based augmented reality system for the Presidents’ Memorabilia at AEA-IRC, DLSU-D. Point your camera at an artifact and it identifies the item and shows its story—nothing to download or install; just open it in your mobile browser.",
      "guide.reply.why":"Here’s why it matters — traditional displays struggle to hold attention and visitation has been low. Sulyap Lasalyano turns a passive gallery visit into an active learning experience, and supports UN Sustainable Development Goal 11.4 by using technology to protect and promote cultural heritage.",
      "guide.reply.scan":"Fun one! Live Scan uses your phone’s camera and a custom-trained YOLOv8 model to recognize memorabilia in real time. Allow camera access, point at an item, then a 3D model and info sheet appear. Try another angle or better lighting if it isn’t recognized.",
      "guide.reply.kg":"Love this part — the Knowledge Graph shows how the collection fits together—links among AEA-IRC, DLSU-D, presidents, years, and artifacts. Open it from the home page, drag to pan, and use +/− to zoom.",
      "guide.reply.browse":"No camera? No problem — browse by DLSU-D president, open memorabilia, and view a rotatable, zoomable 3D model with details.",
      "guide.reply.lang":"Yep! You can read the content in English, Filipino, Spanish, French, Chinese, Korean, or Japanese.",
      "guide.reply.aeairc":"Nice ask — AEA-IRC is a replica of the Aguinaldo Shrine in Kawit—a larger facade version of the shrine. It was the brainchild of Br. Andrew Gonzales and was inaugurated on April 30, 1992. It began in 1977 as a classroom-sized library when the campus was first established.",
      "guide.reply.team":"Proud to say — Sulyap Lasalyano is a thesis project by Lagajino, Ricafrente, and Capistrano (BS Computer Science, Specializing in Intelligent Systems), under adviser Tita R. Herradura.",
      "guide.reply.presidents":"You’ll meet them on the home page — former presidents in the collection story, including Br. Inigo, Br. Andrew, Br. Armin, Br. Donato, Br. Gus, Br. Mawel, Br. Rolly, Br. Sockie, and Dr. Quebengco. Browse their memorabilia from the marquee!",
